Google Sans Text";
mso-bidi-font-family:"Google Sans Text";color:#1B1C1D'> Therefore, the corr=
ect
mental model for an operator is not that of driving a stable vehicle, but of
actively managing a balanced system. Every control input&#8212;accelerating,
braking, turning, lifting, tilting&#8212;is an act of maintaining the syste=
m's
equilibrium within the ever-changing confines of the stability pyramid.</sp=
an><span
lang=3DEN style=3D'color:black'><o:p></o:p></span></p>

