<p class=3DMsoNormal style=3D'margin-bottom:12.0pt;line-height:114%;border:=
none;
mso-padding-alt:31.0pt 31.0pt 31.0pt 31.0pt;mso-border-shadow:yes'><span
lang=3DEN style=3D'font-family:"Google Sans Text";mso-fareast-font-family:"=
Google Sans Text";
mso-bidi-font-family:"Google Sans Text";color:#1B1C1D'>Once the load's phys=
ical
properties are known, the focus shifts to the equipment that will perform t=
he
lift. This evaluation has two equally critical components: ensuring the
equipment has sufficient capacity for the specific lift configuration and v=
erifying
that it is in a safe, serviceable condition, free from defects that could c=
ause
failure under load.</span><span lang=3DEN style=3D'color:black'><o:p></o:p>=
</span></p>

<p class=3DMsoNormal style=3D'margin-bottom:12.0pt;line-height:114%;border:=
none;
