Google Sans Text";
mso-bidi-font-family:"Google Sans Text";color:#1B1C1D'>The analysis reveals=
 a
critical transition in the nature of risk. In manual and basic mechanical
handling, hazards are often overt, such as the ergonomic strain of improper
lifting or the immediate danger of a dropped load. In advanced and automated
systems, the risks become more abstract and insidious. They include invisib=
le
threats like electrostatic discharge, which can destroy sensitive electroni=
cs
without a sound or flash, and latent hazards like stored energy, which can
remain dormant within a machine long after it has been powered down.</span>=
<span
lang=3DEN style=3D'color:black'><o:p></o:p></span></p>

