Google Sans Text";
mso-bidi-font-family:"Google Sans Text";color:#1B1C1D'>In mechatronic syste=
ms,
this principle remains paramount. A robot's control software must account f=
or
the CoG of the object being handled. Crucially, it must also calculate the
combined CoG of the object <i style=3D'mso-bidi-font-style:normal'>and</i> =
the
End-of-Arm Tooling (EOAT) attached to the robot's wrist.</span><sup><span
lang=3DEN style=3D'font-size:12.0pt;line-height:114%;font-family:"Google Sa=
ns Text";
mso-fareast-font-family:"Google Sans Text";mso-bidi-font-family:"Google San=
s Text";
color:#444746'>1</span></sup><span lang=3DEN style=3D'font-family:"Google S=
ans Text";
