color:#1B1C1D'>Shock loading is often called a &quot;silent killer&quot;
because its effects are cumulative and often invisible. Each shock load eve=
nt
can create micro-fractures and accelerate metal fatigue in hooks, links, and
hoist components. Over time, this hidden damage weakens the equipment until=
 it
fails unexpectedly under a load that is well within its stated rated capaci=
ty.</span><sup><span
