:"Google Sans Text";
mso-fareast-font-family:"Google Sans Text";mso-bidi-font-family:"Google San=
s Text";
color:#1B1C1D'> A rigger was preparing a &quot;multi-lift,&quot; a procedure
for hoisting multiple structural members at once. He had already rigged one
50-foot-long bar joist using a choker sling and had the crane operator lift=
 it
approximately 15 feet in the air to provide clearance. As the rigger bent o=
ver
to begin rigging a second joist on the ground, the eye of the choker sling
holding the suspended joist slipped out of the crane hook. The 50-foot steel
joist fell, striking and killing the rigger below.</span><sup><span lang=3D=
EN
style=3D'font-size:12.0pt;line-height:114%;font-family:"Google Sans Text";
