engineering controls. OSHA regulations primarily dictate <i style=3D'mso-bi=
di-font-style:
normal'>how to use, inspect, and maintain that equipment safely in the
workplace</i>, focusing on procedural and administrative controls. One
framework is incomplete without the other. For instance, ASME B30.26 specif=
ies
that a rigging block must be designed to deform before it fails
catastrophically.</span><sup><span lang=3DEN style=3D'font-size:12.0pt;line=
-height:
114%;font-family:"Google Sans Text";mso-fareast-font-family:"Google Sans Te=
xt";
