Google Sans Text";
mso-bidi-font-family:"Google Sans Text";color:#1B1C1D'> Its defining princi=
ple
is its default state. In the absence of electrical power, the springs exert=
 a
constant, strong force that clamps the brake pads together, locking the mot=
or
shaft and preventing any rotation. The brake is, by its nature, always enga=
ged.</span><sup><span
lang=3DEN style=3D'font-size:12.0pt;line-height:114%;font-family:"Google Sa=
ns Text";
mso-fareast-font-family:"Google Sans Text";mso-bidi-font-family:"Google San=
