lang=3DEN style=3D'font-family:"Google Sans Text";mso-fareast-font-family:"=
Google Sans Text";
mso-bidi-font-family:"Google Sans Text";color:#1B1C1D'>However, a second,
equally important objective is the improvement of worker safety.</span><sup=
><span
lang=3DEN style=3D'font-size:12.0pt;line-height:114%;font-family:"Google Sa=
ns Text";
mso-fareast-font-family:"Google Sans Text";mso-bidi-font-family:"Google San=
s Text";
color:#444746'>7</span></sup><span lang=3DEN style=3D'font-family:"Google S=
ans Text";
mso-fareast-font-family:"Google Sans Text";mso-bidi-font-family:"Google San=
s Text";
color:#1B1C1D'> Automation is frequently implemented to remove human workers
from tasks that are tedious, ergonomically hazardous, or inherently dangero=
us.</span><sup><span
lang=3DEN style=3D'font-size:12.0pt;line-height:114%;font-family:"Google Sa=
ns Text";
mso-fareast-font-family:"Google Sans Text";mso-bidi-font-family:"Google San=
s Text";
color:#444746'>6</span></sup><span lang=3DEN style=3D'font-family:"Google S=
ans Text";
mso-fareast-font-family:"Google Sans Text";mso-bidi-font-family:"Google San=
s Text";
color:#1B1C1D'> Robots are assigned to handle hazardous materials, lift hea=
vy
loads that cause musculoskeletal disorders, and perform repetitive motions =
that
lead to strain injuries.</span><sup><span lang=3DEN style=3D'font-size:12.0=
pt;
line-height:114%;font-family:"Google Sans Text";mso-fareast-font-family:"Go=
ogle Sans Text";
mso-bidi-font-family:"Google Sans Text";color:#444746'>1</span></sup><span
lang=3DEN style=3D'font-family:"Google Sans Text";mso-fareast-font-family:"=
Google Sans Text";
mso-bidi-font-family:"Google Sans Text";color:#1B1C1D'> In this sense,
automation is a powerful engineering control designed to mitigate risk. Yet,
this very solution introduces a new and complex set of hazards. The powerfu=
l,
high-speed machines that protect workers from one set of risks create anoth=
er,
requiring a sophisticated and holistic approach to safety management.
Automation is therefore both a solution to and a source of safety challenge=
s,
and a comprehensive understanding of mechatronic safety requires acknowledg=
ing
this duality.</span><span lang=3DEN style=3D'color:black'><o:p></o:p></span=
></p>

