e,
presenting risks of shock, arc flash, and fire from power supplies, control
cabinets, and cabling.</span><sup><span lang=3DEN style=3D'font-size:12.0pt;
line-height:114%;font-family:"Google Sans Text";mso-fareast-font-family:"Go=
ogle Sans Text";
mso-bidi-font-family:"Google Sans Text";color:#444746'>9</span></sup><span
lang=3DEN style=3D'font-family:"Google Sans Text";mso-fareast-font-family:"=
Google Sans Text";
mso-bidi-font-family:"Google Sans Text";color:#1B1C1D'> Many powerful syste=
ms,
such as large robotic arms or cranes, utilize hydraulic systems. A ruptured
hydraulic line can release a high-pressure stream of fluid capable of causi=
ng
severe injection injuries, and the fluid itself may be flammable or toxic.<=
/span><sup><span
lang=3DEN style=3D'font-size:12.0pt;line-height:114%;font-family:"Google Sa=
ns Text";
mso-fareast-font-family:"Google Sans Text";mso-bidi-font-family:"Google San=
s Text";
color:#444746'>9</span></sup><span lang=3DEN style=3D'font-family:"Google S=
ans Text";
mso-fareast-font-family:"Google Sans Text";mso-bidi-font-family:"Google San=
s Text";
color:#1B1C1D'> Similarly, pneumatic systems, which use compressed air, can
create hazards from whipping hoses if a line fails.</span><sup><span lang=
=3DEN
style=3D'font-size:12.0pt;line-height:114%;font-family:"Google Sans Text";
mso-fareast-font-family:"Google Sans Text";mso-bidi-font-family:"Google San=
s Text";
color:#444746'>9</span></sup><span lang=3DEN style=3D'color:black'><o:p></o=
:p></span></p>

<p class=3DMsoNormal style=3D'margin-bottom:12.0pt;line-height:114%;border:=
none;
mso-padding-alt:31.0pt 31.0pt 31.0pt 31.0pt;mso-border-shadow:yes'><span
lang=3DEN style=3D'font-family:"Google Sans Text";mso-fareast-font-family:"=
Google Sans Text";
mso-bidi-font-family:"Google Sans Text";color:#1B1C1D'>Third are the <b
