lly
removed their own locks. For larger jobs involving many workers, a group
lockbox is used. A single lock is placed on the equipment's disconnect, and=
 the
key to that lock is placed inside the box. Each worker then places their
personal lock on the box itself. The key to the equipment cannot be accessed
until every single worker has removed their personal lock from the box. This
ensures that the last person to finish their work is protected, creating a
