s Text";
color:#1B1C1D'> An overhead crane, also known as a bridge crane, consists o=
f a <b
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-weight:normal'>bridge</b>, which is the primary hori=
zontal
beam, or girder, that spans the width of the work area, such as a factory b=
ay
or a stockyard.</span><sup><span lang=3DEN style=3D'font-size:12.0pt;line-h=
eight:
114%;font-family:"Google Sans Text";mso-fareast-font-family:"Google Sans Te=
xt";
