Google Sans Text";
mso-bidi-font-family:"Google Sans Text";color:#1B1C1D'>A safe lift is a
carefully managed exercise in physics and procedural discipline. The first =
and
most inviolable rule is to <b style=3D'mso-bidi-font-weight:normal'>underst=
and
the load</b>. The operator must know the precise weight of the load to be
lifted and confirm that it does not exceed the crane's rated load-carrying
capacity, which must be clearly marked on the crane itself.</span><sup><span
lang=3DEN style=3D'font-size:12.0pt;line-height:114%;font-family:"Google Sa=
ns Text";
mso-fareast-font-family:"Google Sans Text";mso-bidi-font-family:"Google San=
s Text";
color:#444746'>12</span></sup><span lang=3DEN style=3D'font-family:"Google =
Sans Text";
mso-fareast-font-family:"Google Sans Text";mso-bidi-font-family:"Google San=
s Text";
color:#1B1C1D'> Attempting to lift an unknown weight or exceeding the rated
load is one of the most common causes of catastrophic crane failure.</span>=
<sup><span
lang=3DEN style=3D'font-size:12.0pt;line-height:114%;font-family:"Google Sa=
ns Text";
mso-fareast-font-family:"Google Sans Text";mso-bidi-font-family:"Google San=
s Text";
color:#444746'>24</span></sup><span lang=3DEN style=3D'color:black'><o:p></=
o:p></span></p>

<p class=3DMsoNormal style=3D'margin-bottom:12.0pt;line-height:114%;border:=
none;
mso-padding-alt:31.0pt 31.0pt 31.0pt 31.0pt;mso-border-shadow:yes'><span
lang=3DEN style=3D'font-family:"Google Sans Text";mso-fareast-font-family:"=
Google Sans Text";
mso-bidi-font-family:"Google Sans Text";color:#1B1C1D'>The manner in which =
the
load is lifted is equally critical. Crane controls must be operated smoothl=
y to
avoid <b style=3D'mso-bidi-font-weight:normal'>shock loading</b> and <b
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-weight:normal'>jerky movements</b>.</span><sup><span
lang=3DEN style=3D'font-size:12.0pt;line-height:114%;font-family:"Google Sa=
ns Text";
mso-fareast-font-family:"Google Sans Text";mso-bidi-font-family:"Google San=
s Text";
color:#444746'>27</span></sup><span lang=3DEN style=3D'font-family:"Google =
Sans Text";
mso-fareast-font-family:"Google Sans Text";mso-bidi-font-family:"Google San=
s Text";
color:#1B1C1D'> A sudden start or stop of the hoist or a jerky movement of =
the
bridge or trolley can dramatically increase the dynamic forces acting on the
wire rope and the crane's structure. These forces can be many times greater
than the static weight of the load, potentially leading to the failure of a
component that would be perfectly safe under a smooth, controlled lift.</sp=
an><sup><span
lang=3DEN style=3D'font-size:12.0pt;line-height:114%;font-family:"Google Sa=
