The red-tagging and reporting protocol is the critical administrative contr=
ol
that closes this safety loop. It is the formal procedure that transforms an
individual operator's findings into a structured, organizational response,
ensuring that a known hazard is mitigated before it can cause harm. This
protocol is the bridge between risk identification and risk control, a
fundamental principle in any effective safety management system.</span><span
lang=3DEN style=3D'color:black'><o:p></o:p></span></p>

